# ============================================================ # ZOMATO NOTES - ALGORITHMS # Part 2: Integrated Ranking Engine # ============================================================ # ============================================================ # REQUIRED FUNCTION 1 # INSERTION SORT BY NUMERIC KEY # ============================================================ def insertion_sort_by_key(items: list[dict], key: str) -> list[dict]: """ Sort dictionaries in descending order by a numeric key. This is implemented manually using insertion sort. No sorted() or list.sort() is used. """ result = items.copy() for i in range(1, len(result)): current = result[i] j = i - 1 while j >= 0 and result[j][key] < current[key]: result[j + 1] = result[j] j -= 1 result[j + 1] = current return result # ============================================================ # REQUIRED FUNCTION 2 # ITERATIVE BINARY SEARCH # ============================================================ def binary_search_iterative( sorted_titles: list[str], target: str ) -> int: """ Search for an exact title in an alphabetically sorted list. Returns: index if found -1 if not found """ left = 0 right = len(sorted_titles) - 1 target = target.lower() while left <= right: # Overflow-safe midpoint formula mid = left + (right - left) // 2 current = sorted_titles[mid].lower() if current == target: return mid elif current < target: left = mid + 1 else: right = mid - 1 return -1 # ============================================================ # REQUIRED FUNCTION 3 # RECURSIVE BINARY SEARCH # ============================================================ def binary_search_recursive( sorted_titles: list[str], target: str, start: int, end: int ) -> int: """ Recursive binary search for an exact title. Returns: index if found -1 if not found """ # Explicit base case if start > end: return -1 mid = start + (end - start) // 2 current = sorted_titles[mid].lower() target = target.lower() if current == target: return mid elif current < target: return binary_search_recursive( sorted_titles, target, mid + 1, end ) else: return binary_search_recursive( sorted_titles, target, start, mid - 1 ) # ============================================================ # REQUIRED FUNCTION 4 # LINEAR SEARCH WITH FOUND FLAG # ============================================================ def linear_search( items: list[dict], key: str, value ) -> dict | None: """ Sequentially searches for the first matching dictionary. Returns: matching dictionary None if no match exists """ found = False result = None for item in items: if item.get(key) == value: result = item found = True break if found: return result return None # ============================================================ # EXISTING FUNCTION # INSERTION SORT BY TITLE # ============================================================ def insertion_sort(notes): """ Existing helper. Sort notes alphabetically by title. """ sorted_notes = notes.copy() for i in range(1, len(sorted_notes)): key = sorted_notes[i] j = i - 1 while ( j >= 0 and sorted_notes[j]["title"].lower() > key["title"].lower() ): sorted_notes[j + 1] = sorted_notes[j] j -= 1 sorted_notes[j + 1] = key return sorted_notes # ============================================================ # EXISTING FUNCTION # BINARY SEARCH TITLE # ============================================================ def binary_search_title(sorted_notes, title): """ Existing helper. Finds all notes having the requested title. """ title = title.lower() left = 0 right = len(sorted_notes) - 1 while left <= right: mid = (left + right) // 2 current = sorted_notes[mid]["title"].lower() if current == title: result = [] start = mid while ( start > 0 and sorted_notes[start - 1]["title"].lower() == title ): start -= 1 while start < len(sorted_notes): if sorted_notes[start]["title"].lower() != title: break result.append(sorted_notes[start]) start += 1 return result elif current < title: left = mid + 1 else: right = mid - 1 return [] # ============================================================ # EXISTING FUNCTION # BINARY SEARCH TAG # ============================================================ def binary_search_tag(sorted_notes, tag): """ Existing helper. Finds all notes having the requested tag. """ tag = tag.lower() left = 0 right = len(sorted_notes) - 1 while left <= right: mid = (left + right) // 2 current = sorted_notes[mid]["tag"].lower() if current == tag: start = mid while ( start > 0 and sorted_notes[start - 1]["tag"].lower() == tag ): start -= 1 result = [] while start < len(sorted_notes): if sorted_notes[start]["tag"].lower() != tag: break result.append(sorted_notes[start]) start += 1 return result elif current < tag: left = mid + 1 else: right = mid - 1 return [] # ============================================================ # EXISTING FUNCTION # LINEAR SEARCH TAG # ============================================================ def linear_search_tag(notes, tag): """ Existing helper. Returns all notes matching the tag. """ tag = tag.lower() result = [] for note in notes: if note["tag"].lower() == tag: result.append(note) return result